# Logs
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

node_modules
# `dist/*`, not `dist`: git will not re-include a file whose parent directory
# is excluded, so the negation below only works if the directory itself stays
# unignored.
dist/*
dist-ssr
*.local

# ...except the shipped embed bundle. Consumers install this package straight
# from git (`github:dappros/ai-assistant-ui#<sha>`), and npm only builds a git
# dependency if the package has a `prepare` script. This one cannot have a
# working one: the build resolves @ethora/chat-component from the SIBLING
# checkout (../ethora-chat-component/src, see vite.config.ts), and the
# published chat-component tarball ships only `dist`, no sources. So the built
# file has to be in the tree, or a git install silently yields a package whose
# "main" points at nothing.
#
# Update it with `npx vite build --minify false` and commit the result in the
# same commit as the version bump.
!dist/ethora_assistant.js

